  title={Transformer-Based Title Generation for Pashto Texts Using Topic Modeling Techniques}, 
  year={2025},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={1-7},
  abstract={This study proposes a transformer-assisted framework for automatic title generation in Pashto, a low-resource language with limited NLP resources. The approach combines topic modeling techniques with a generative transformer to produce coherent and contextually meaningful titles for news articles. A custom corpus of 10,252 Pashto news items was collected from major online outlets and preprocessed using Bag-of-Words (BoW) and Term Frequency–Inverse Document Frequency (TF-IDF) representations. Five topic-modeling algorithms; Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA), Latent Semantic Analysis (LSA), Non-negative Matrix Factorization (NMF), Hierarchical Dirichlet Process (HDP), and BERTopic, were compared to identify the most coherent latent structures. Topics extracted from these models were used to guide title generation using the GPT-4o language model. Evaluations based on topic coherence and ROUGE metrics indicate that HDP with TF-IDF achieved the highest in terms of coherence and ROUGE-L, while NMF performed best with BoW. The findings demonstrate that combining probabilistic topic modeling with generative transformers can improve automatic title generation for under-resourced languages and establish a baseline for future Pashto NLP research.},
  keywords={Measurement;Adaptation models;Semantics;Merging;Coherence;Transformers;Probabilistic logic;Multilingual;Resource management;Context modeling;Topic Modeling;Title Generation},
